; Interprets: RFC 8583
;; What RFC 8583's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. The document defines no command: the Load AVP rides every
;; application's answers through their * [ AVP ], so a block here has no
;; scope, and holds wherever a document reading the AVP reads it.


;; A load report is an endpoint's (section 6.1.1) or an agent's (6.1.2),
;; and each holds the three members, so the rules hold of every Load; they
;; are written once, here, and section 6.1.2's same sentences of an agent's
;; report are recorded below, read by these rules. Whose DiameterIdentity
;; the SourceID holds, and the Load-Type, HOST for an endpoint and PEER for
;; an agent, are the sender's role, which the message does not show.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: load-endpoint-members
; AVP: Load
; Section: 6.1.1
"The Diameter endpoint MUST include its own DiameterIdentity in the SourceID AVP included in the Load AVP."
    members at-least-one SourceID
"The Diameter endpoint MUST include a Load-Type AVP of type \"HOST\" in the Load AVP."
    members at-least-one Load-Type
"The Diameter endpoint MUST include its Load value in the Load-Value AVP in the Load AVP."
    members at-least-one Load-Value


;; Read by section 6.1.1's block, whose rules hold of every Load.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: load-agent-members
; AVP: Load
; Section: 6.1.2
"The Diameter Agent MUST include its own DiameterIdentity in the SourceID AVP included in the Load AVP."
    text-only
"The Diameter Agent MUST include a Load-Type AVP of type \"PEER\" in the Load AVP."
    text-only
"The Diameter Agent MUST include its Load value in the Load-Value AVP in the Load AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: load-value-range
; AVP: Load-Value
; Section: 7.3
"The Load value has a range of 0-65535."
    range 0..65535
